From 84e70cea0917b4b20c981b06bcc50aecc7e76e6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add UICapture widget: capture the game screen into memory for
 UI backgrounds

UICapture copies what has been drawn so far (the game and the UI behind
it) into a GPU texture and draws it in its rect, for pause and menu
backgrounds. Nothing is written to disk.

- timing: OnShow (once when shown, a frozen frame) / EveryFrame / Script
  (Capture())
- area: Screen (whole screen) / Behind (only the area behind the widget)
- color tint, blur (repeated half-size downsampling, no shader),
  blockInput, previewTexture for designers
- GetCapturedTexture() / ReleaseCapture() for scripts

RenderCommand gets CopyFramebufferToTexture (via glBlitFramebuffer, so
MSAA screens work) and BlitTexture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
